meta {
  name: Verify Email
  type: http
  seq: 6
}

post {
  url: {{base_url}}/v1/auth/verify-email
  body: json
  auth: none
}

body:json {
  {
    "token": "paste-verification-token-here"
  }
}

docs {
  Unauthenticated: the token identifies the user. It has to be — the address is verified
  *before* the user can meaningfully sign in.

  The token arrives by email. In local dev, read it from the `outbox_worker` container logs.
  The link in the email is `GET /v1/auth/verify-email?token=…`, which does the same thing and
  renders a result page.

  Only the SHA-256 of the token is stored, so you cannot recover it from the database.
}
